# Environment Variables Setup - Waná Marketplace 2026

## 0. Waná API (Phase 0 — Docker stack)

```bash
# Waná REST API (Fastify + PostgreSQL)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Must match api JWT_SECRET (middleware validates session cookie)
JWT_SECRET=wana_dev_jwt_secret_change_in_production

# Stripe (frontend publishable key — must match API)
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Payments mock mode (must match api PAYMENTS_MODE=mock for local dev)
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_MODE=mock

# Marketing (Fase 4)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# Local PostgreSQL (docker compose)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wana:wana_dev_password@localhost:5432/wana?schema=public
```

Login demo accounts (after `npm run api:seed`): guest@wana.local, host@wana.local, admin@wana.local — password `wana12345`

Start infrastructure: `npm run docker:infra` then `npm run api:migrate && npm run api:seed && npm run api:dev`

## 2. Alegra (Invoicing) Configuration

```bash
ALEGRA_EMAIL=tu-email@alegra.com
ALEGRA_API_TOKEN=your-alegra-api-token-here
```

Get these from:
1. Go to https://alegra.com/api/docs
2. Create API token in your account settings
3. Use your registered email and token

**Important**: If not configured, the system will fall back to `pending_invoices` table for manual processing.

## 3. Payment Gateway (Bold/Stripe) Configuration

```bash
# Bold (Recommended for Colombia)
BOLD_API_KEY=sk_live_xxxxx
BOLD_API_SECRET=secret_xxxxx
BOLD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxx

# Or Stripe Alternative
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_xxxxx
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_xxxxx
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxx
```

Get these from:
- Bold: https://dashboard.bold.co/api-keys
- Stripe: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys

## 4. Upstash (Rate Limiting) Configuration

```bash
# Upstash Redis for Rate Limiting
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-instance.upstash.io
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your_rest_token_here
```

Setup:
1. Go to https://console.upstash.com/redis
2. Create a new Redis database
3. Copy REST URL and Token from console

## 5. Authentication Configuration

```bash
# NextAuth / JWT (if using custom auth)
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your-secret-here
NEXTAUTH_URL=https://yourdomain.com

# Or GitHub OAuth
GITHUB_ID=your_github_app_id
GITHUB_SECRET=your_github_secret
```

## 6. Admin Configuration

```bash
# Admin emails (comma-separated)
ADMIN_EMAILS=admin@example.com,support@wana.com

# Webhook signing secret
WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=whsec_xxxxxx
```

## 7. Production Settings

```bash
# Environment
NODE_ENV=production

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=info
SENTRY_DSN=https://xxxxx@sentry.io/xxxxxx
```

## Database Schema Requirements

Before running the app, ensure these tables exist in Supabase:

### domos
```sql
id: uuid PRIMARY KEY
nombre: text
descripcion: text
precio_por_noche: numeric
estado: text (disponible|ocupado|mantenimiento)
owner_id: uuid FK users
created_at: timestamp
```

### bookings
```sql
id: uuid PRIMARY KEY
property_id: uuid FK domos
guest_id: uuid FK users
guest_email: text
guest_name: text
check_in: date
days: integer
status: text (pending_payment|confirmed|completed|cancelled)
fees_breakdown: jsonb
transaction_id: text
invoice_id: text
created_at: timestamp
```

### pending_invoices
```sql
id: uuid PRIMARY KEY
booking_id: uuid FK bookings
transaction_id: text
invoice_data: jsonb
guest_email: text
guest_name: text
status: text (pending|processed|failed)
alegra_error: text (nullable)
created_at: timestamp
```

### audit_logs
```sql
id: uuid PRIMARY KEY
booking_id: uuid FK bookings
transaction_id: text
action: text
fees_breakdown: jsonb
status: text (success|pending_invoice|failed)
method: text (alegra|backup|manual)
timestamp: timestamp
```

### user_roles (RBAC)
```sql
id: uuid PRIMARY KEY
user_id: uuid FK auth.users
role: text (user|host|admin)
created_at: timestamp
UNIQUE(user_id, role)
```

## RLS Policies

Execute the SQL policies from `database/rls-policies.sql`:

1. In Supabase Dashboard, go to SQL Editor
2. Create new query
3. Copy content from `database/rls-policies.sql`
4. Run all queries

Verify RLS is enabled:
```sql
SELECT tablename, rowsecurity FROM pg_tables 
WHERE tablename IN ('domos', 'bookings', 'pending_invoices', 'audit_logs');
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Supabase URL and API keys configured
- [ ] Alegra email and token (optional, but recommended)
- [ ] Payment gateway (Bold or Stripe) keys set
- [ ] Upstash Redis configured for rate limiting
- [ ] Database tables created
- [ ] RLS policies applied
- [ ] Environment variables in `.env.local` and deployment platform

## Security Notes

- **Never commit `.env.local` to version control**
- Use `.env.example` for documentation
- Rotate API keys regularly
- Monitor audit logs for suspicious activity
- Test rate limiting in staging before production
- Validate all incoming payment data server-side

## Support

For issues:
1. Check Supabase logs: Dashboard > Logs
2. Review rate limiting: Upstash Dashboard > Metrics
3. Verify Alegra integration: Alegra Dashboard > API Logs
4. Check application logs: `npm run logs` (if using Vercel)
